  "result": "```json\n{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#37859\", \"PowerToys#46888\", \"PowerToys#46873\"], \"answer\": \"This crash has been reported before. PowerToys#37859 is the main ticket, and the others were closed as duplicates of it. The stack trace matches yours: a NullReferenceException in BindingExpression.SetupDefaultValueConverter, raised while WPF handles a system theme change (ThemeManager.OnSystemThemeChanged). Reporters hit it after waking from sleep or hibernation, after unlocking the PC, or when the display setup changed. A reporter in PowerToys#45219 suspected a day/night auto theme-switching tool running after wake-up. The archive has no fix and no confirmed workaround. The original reporter said it was a one-time crash. After the crash window appears, you can restart PowerToys and carry on, and nothing is lost. If it keeps happening, add your version (0.98.1.0), your OS build and when it happened to PowerToys#37859. If you use an automatic light/dark theme switcher, try turning it off to see whether the crashes stop.\"}\n```",
